      "content": "2.1 Location and Physical Features"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The geography of Tamil Nadu includes location, physical features, climate variations, and district-level distribution.",
        "The state is broadly split into three major physiographic divisions: The Western Ghats, The Eastern Coastal Plains, and The Deccan Plateau.",
        "Hydro-geographic features comprise major river systems alongside key dams and reservoirs critical for the region.",
        "Natural heritage and economic geography cover national parks, wildlife sanctuaries, and mineral resource distribution."
      ],
      "id": "8dlszif"
